      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 5.86,
          "en": "So, it's time for some error handling.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.86,
          "end": 8.71,
          "en": "For example, here when we're logging in,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.71,
          "end": 12.93,
          "en": "I could enter an email address which is technically correct",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.93,
          "end": 15.8,
          "en": "but which wasn't registered on the backend before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.8,
          "end": 19.14,
          "en": "Here I have no user on the backend with that email address",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.14,
          "end": 20.82,
          "en": "but if I try this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.82,
          "end": 23.41,
          "en": "well, I get stuck here on loading screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.41,
          "end": 26.86,
          "en": "because we do get an error response actually.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.86,
          "end": 29.93,
          "en": "And that's why we get this warning here at the bottom",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.93,
          "end": 33.53,
          "en": "but we don't handle that here on the frontend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.53,
          "end": 36.19,
          "en": "And that is of course, something I wanna change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.19,
          "end": 39.16,
          "en": "We want to handle such errors properly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.16,
          "end": 42.16,
          "en": "For this, we can wrap this log in function call",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.16,
          "end": 45.6,
          "en": "with try catch as we did it earlier in the course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.6,
          "end": 48.323,
          "en": "in the Http course section already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.58,
          "end": 51.75,
          "en": "Now we can catch a potential error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.75,
          "end": 53.13,
          "en": "And now it's up to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.13,
          "end": 56.15,
          "en": "what you want to do with such an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.15,
          "end": 58.35,
          "en": "You could add an error overlay.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.35,
          "end": 60.26,
          "en": "You could change the user interface.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.26,
          "end": 63.04,
          "en": "You can do whatever you want here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.04,
          "end": 65.983,
          "en": "I will simply call alert.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.07,
          "end": 71.1,
          "en": "So, the alert API built into React Native",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.1,
          "end": 73.6,
          "en": "which we also used before in the course already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.6,
          "end": 77.89,
          "en": "And on this alert API, I'm going to use the alert method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.89,
          "end": 80.46000000000001,
          "en": "This allows me to show an alert dialogue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.46000000000001,
          "end": 82.8,
          "en": "and there we can set a title.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 82.8,
          "end": 85.52,
          "en": "For example, authentication failed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.49,
          "end": 91.03999999999999,
          "en": "and a message that could say, \"Could not log you in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.03999999999999,
          "end": 94.253,
          "en": "Please check your credentials,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.28999999999999,
          "end": 97.83,
          "en": "or try again later!\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.83,
          "end": 99.453,
          "en": "In case it's a technical error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.03,
          "end": 103.53999999999999,
          "en": "Now you can be more elaborate than that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 103.53999999999999,
          "end": 106.39,
          "en": "You could look into the error response data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.39,
          "end": 109.03999999999999,
          "en": "and see which kind of error you got back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 109.03999999999999,
          "end": 112.81,
          "en": "because Firebase will be sending back different error codes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 112.81,
          "end": 115.55,
          "en": "As you can learn here in the official docs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 115.55,
          "end": 118.45,
          "en": "So, you can show more meaningful error messages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 118.45,
          "end": 121.08,
          "en": "depending on the error you got back.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 121.08,
          "end": 124.16,
          "en": "But here I'll show this generic error message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 124.16,
          "end": 127.303,
          "en": "And with that, if we save this and we restart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.23,
          "end": 131.77,
          "en": "Now if I try to log in with an invalid email address",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 131.77,
          "end": 135.6,
          "en": "so technically valid, but not known on the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 135.6,
          "end": 138.48,
          "en": "I get this alert and I can try again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 138.48,
          "end": 143.05,
          "en": "The same happens if I actually enter an invalid password.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 143.05,
          "end": 145.203,
          "en": "I get this alert and I can try again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 146.16,
          "end": 148.82,
          "en": "Again, you can improve this error handling.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 148.82,
          "end": 151.03,
          "en": "You can handle errors differently",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 151.03,
          "end": 154.87,
          "en": "but this shows you how you can in general handle errors",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 154.87,
          "end": 156.85,
          "en": "and that you should handle them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 156.85,
          "end": 159.99,
          "en": "Because unlike before in the Http section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 159.99,
          "end": 163.3,
          "en": "here it's not just about technical errors",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 163.3,
          "end": 165.84,
          "en": "or missing internet connectivity",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 165.84,
          "end": 167.57,
          "en": "though that could happen as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 167.57,
          "end": 171.083,
          "en": "But here it's also about handling invalid credentials.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 172.15,
          "end": 174.55,
          "en": "Now you might want to add that same error handling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 174.55,
          "end": 177.87,
          "en": "on the signup screen and wrap create user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 177.87,
          "end": 179.71,
          "en": "with try catch here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 182.94,
          "end": 186.89,
          "en": "so that if something goes wrong here, we also show an alert.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 186.89,
          "end": 189.87,
          "en": "So, for that I'm also going to import alert here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 189.87,
          "end": 191.27,
          "en": "call that alert method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 191.27,
          "end": 194.713,
          "en": "And then I also say, \"Authentication failed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 196.3,
          "end": 198.59,
          "en": "Could not create user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 198.59,
          "end": 203.59,
          "en": "please check your input and try again later.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 204.11,
          "end": 206.55,
          "en": "Anything like this could be used here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 206.55,
          "end": 209.883,
          "en": "to show an error message if signup fails.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 211.2,
          "end": 213.28,
          "en": "And that's some basic error handling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 213.28,
          "end": 216.56,
          "en": "which I want to add here before we now move on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 216.56,
          "end": 219.36,
          "en": "And we now make sure that we do something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 219.36,
